{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"body":"Correction to the measurement comment: change 2451 (artifact 2752-8c0f-84a8-4cdb) is not a clean case. At the reviewed revision \"Section-1.5\" appears only at structural-guards.md:129, while the finding's own evidence says line 119 also references it. The veto there tested the finding's own (partly wrong) evidence. Confirmed correct findings dropped: 4 (changes 1547, 1428 PS1, 1428 PS2, 3056).\n\nReproduction on the current verifier settings (standard class = bedrock sonnet-4-6, temperature 0, agentic; prompt swapped by file copy, no stash). Live verifier calls total: 15.\n- Synthetic fixture (diff adding a doc line with a wrong line anchor and a dangling section ref, plus a control whose own evidence is wrong): unfixed prompt spared both correct findings in 4/4 runs; control vetoed 4/4. Does not reproduce.\n- Real replay, merged form of 1428 (6c8daf79457, ADR 0059:132 still cites capabilities.py:186-206; table at 317), saved finding + control: unfixed prompt spared the finding 3/3; control vetoed 3/3. Does not reproduce.\n- Real replay, Gerrit 1428 PS2 (fd83b7c863b) with assembled diff context: unfixed prompt vetoed the finding 1/3 (cra=no) and spared it 2/3; fixed prompt spared it 3/3 (cra=yes).\n- Real replay, 2451 PS1: vetoed on both prompts with eef=no (consistent with the correction above).\n\nThe saved drops record verdict model opus-4-8; whether the Pass-2 verifier ran on that model at the time is unchecked.\n\nWork in progress (uncommitted, worktree fix-code-review-veto-scope): scoped cited_reference_accurate rule in code-review-verify.md; live test replaying 6c8daf79457. That test passes on both prompts, so AC 3 (\"fails on the unfixed prompt\") is not met. Paused for an operator decision on the test form."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793512829148619001,"uuid":"0766154d-dce0-454d-